  "body": "Verification messages can be sent either in a room shared by the two parties.\r\nThere is a part not covered in the documentation that is signicantly different between to_device and room.\r\n\r\nIt's when requesting (`m.key.verification.request`), the requests is sent to several devices (as several to_device or as one room message).\r\nThe spec says\r\n> When Bob[..] accepts the verification on one of his devices (sending [..] an m.key.verification.ready [..]), Alice will send an m.key.verification.cancel event to Bob’s other devices with a code of m.accepted [..].\r\n\r\n<img width=\"771\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/9841565/199020620-1084ff96-2fc7-45e0-bc3e-7b645417ffef.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\nThis actually only applies to to_device verification.\r\n\r\nIf the verification is performed in a room, no cancel event should be sent at all when the request is readied.\r\nInstead Bob's other devices when seeing a `m.key.verification.ready` sent from another of bob's own device should enter a passive mode and stop interacting with this verification at all (to prevent sending cancel for unexpected events).\r\n\r\n",
